<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sugu-Okamoto</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sugu-Okamoto site</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sugu-Okamoto is an archaeological site in Kasuga, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka-prefecture">Fukuoka Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, regarded as the centre of the Yayoi-period state of Na. Excavations since 1899 have found jar burials with Chinese bronze mirrors, bronze weapons and glass ornaments, above all in a rich grave of the 1st century BCE. The finds point to a powerful local elite with links to Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and are central to studies of early state formation in Japan.</p></div>
